Z||000000||BV MotorSports||09-29-2001||12:37 AM||||I rememebr a guy going into detail about using the syclone ECM for a turbocharged fiero application but I cant seem to find it. What was needed and any info would be outstanding!<P>Also, any ideas why my 87 GT would pop out of first gear when I come to a complete stop and push it into first (I can feel it not wanting to go completely into 1st) it will just sit there till I try to pull out and then "grrrr" it goes back into neutral. Sometimes I have to try to move the car a bit in 2nd then shift it up into 1st. I hate that! I have adjusted the shifter cables till I am blue in the face w/ no luck. Maybe the cable is stretched?<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||09-29-2001||12:45 AM||||Have you tried doing a search for "Syclone" or "7749"?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-29-2001||06:20 PM||||I've got the '749 ecm and Syclone prom in my Fiero. It was a mistake on my part to come out and recommend this combination to anyone. For me, it has been a very smooth and reliable setup, but PLEASE don't make this kind of swap unless you have someone to work with tuning the chips. The stock settings in the prom are way off from where they need to be for the Fiero and would more than likely toast an engine if you tried to run it "as is". I have been running this ecm for several months and I have made at least 50 prom changes, and it still needs a little more tweaking. I have been very lucky so far, but my luck may not extend to you. If I ever get the setup "perfect", then I will let everyone know, but until then I am going to quietly keep working on the supercharged 3.4||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-29-2001||08:56 PM||||Testify Brother!||||reg||1
Z||000004||BV MotorSports||09-29-2001||10:21 PM||||Fair enuff Cooter. Thanks for the heads up. The reason I asked is that a guy on the StarQuest MSG board wants to convert his Conquest over to MPI using the Aus. issue Sigma/Magna fuel injection set up. he was planning on using a modified GM ECU. <BR>I passed on the info from some posts I found. I told him it would be ALOT simpler to use Haltech, TEC II or SDS F/I set up.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
